<?xml version="1.0"?>
<system name="rain"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSimSystem.xsd">

<!-- ===================================================================
     Rain factors (core/environment/rain.py).

     Two multipliers and the liquid water content. core/control/derive.py
     wraps EVERY <function> of the airframe's LIFT and DRAG axes in a
     <product> with the axis's factor (the icing injection's form), and
     adds an <external_reactions> force "rain-momentum" in the BODY frame
     at the aerodynamic reference point. The rain provider writes the
     factors from a stated linear mapping in the liquid water content and
     the force's direction and magnitude from the drops the aircraft
     sweeps up, every step. Nothing here maps the rain to the numbers:
     the LWC is declared so the provider has one property to write and
     the record one value to read back.

     NEUTRAL VALUES: both factors 1.0 and the force's magnitude 0 (x * 1.0
     and x + 0.0 are exact in IEEE 754, so the derived airframe flies
     bit-identically to the stock one; measured in tests/test_rain.py),
     LWC 0.

     NOT CLAIMED: the factors scale whole axes (the measured effect is on
     maximum lift); no airframe's rain response is validated.
     =================================================================== -->

  <property value="1.0">rain/lift-factor</property>
  <property value="1.0">rain/drag-factor</property>
  <property value="0.0">rain/lwc-gm3</property>

</system>
